# typescript-go-cs

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **This is a proof of what the [go2cs](https://github.com/ritchiecarroll/go2cs) transpiler can do. It is NOT a
> replacement for the TypeScript compiler.** Do not use it to compile TypeScript. Use
> [TypeScript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) itself.

> [!WARNING]
> **Not affiliated with or endorsed by Microsoft.** TypeScript is a trademark of Microsoft Corporation. This is an
> unofficial C# conversion of part of TypeScript's Go source, made with go2cs and published by the go2cs project.

## What it shows

go2cs converted TypeScript's own Go compiler packages (scanner, parser, binder, checker, printer, transformers and
the program that ties them together), at
[microsoft/TypeScript `{{TS_SHORT}}`](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/tree/{{TS_COMMIT}}/tsc), to C#.
{{HEADLINE}} These results were measured on {{PLATFORM}} on {{DATE}}:

<!-- typescript-go-cs:results -->
| What was compared | Inputs | Result |
|:--|:--|:--|
| Parse demo: diagnostics and every syntax node with its position | `samples/good.ts`, `samples/bad.ts` | {{PARSE_DEMO}} |
| Parser corpus: the inputs of TypeScript's own parser fuzz test | {{CORPUS_UNITS}} files | {{CORPUS_RESULT}} |
| Type-check demo: every diagnostic of a type-checked program | `samples/check.ts`, `samples/good.ts` | {{CHECK_DEMO}} |
| Type-check, TypeScript's compiler tests: each file checked alone, every diagnostic | {{TC_UNITS}} files | {{TC_RESULT}} |
| Emit, TypeScript's compiler tests: each file's JavaScript and `.d.ts` | {{EM_UNITS}} files | {{EM_RESULT}} |
| Emit demo | `samples/good.ts`, `bad.ts`, `emit.ts` | {{EMIT_DEMO}} |
| Multi-file projects: `tsconfig.json`, every diagnostic, every output file | `samples/projects/shop`, `legacy` | {{MF_RESULT}} |

A result is "identical" only when the converted program's output equals the native Go build's output byte for byte.
[PROOF.md](PROOF.md) has the method, both sides' outputs and every figure above.
<!-- /typescript-go-cs:results -->

Inputs use LF line endings, as git stores them; byte counts and hashes in this repository assume that.

## What is not here

The language service, the language server, `tsc`'s command line and watch mode are not converted here. Five of
TypeScript's packages (`internal/ls`, `internal/ls/lsconv`, `internal/ls/autoimport`, `internal/project` and
`internal/fourslash`) use a generic-constraint shape go2cs does not convert yet, and everything that imports them is
left out with them.

